%% element-pool: per-control lifecycle as Mount/Unmount move it through
%% the per-type pool. The "compositor-tainted" terminal state is what
%% drops a control out of pooling permanently.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Pooled: new (first mount path falls through to ctor)
    Pooled --> Rented: Reconciler.Mount → pool.TryRent
    Rented --> Returning: Reconciler.Unmount → pool.Return
    Returning --> Pooled: ForceDetach + CleanElement, stack &lt; cap
    Returning --> [*]: cap reached (32 / type) → GC eligible
    Returning --> [*]: compositor-tainted → never re-pooled
    Pooled --> [*]: ElementPool.Dispose → Clear()
